            {'id': '01f106b0f8dd1810a160923a79011d8d', 'content': ['- "On-time" means the delivery was completed within 2 hours after the scheduled time: delivered_at <= scheduled_at + INTERVAL 2 HOURS. On-time rate is the percentage of deliveries that meet this rule.\n', '\n', '- All monetary amounts (revenue, cost) are in USD. Use columns revenue_usd and cost_usd. When presenting money or percentages, round to 2 decimal places.\n', '\n', '- When asked about "deliveries",
                    "runs",
                    "completed" runs, or "fulfilled" orders, use the delivery_runs table and only count rows where status = \'delivered\'. Do not include cancelled or in-transit runs in counts or averages.\n', '\n', '- Join drivers to delivery_runs on driver_id; depots to delivery_runs on depot_id; regions to depots on region_id. Customers link to delivery_runs via customer_id.\n', '\n', '- For "revenue by region",
                    "deliveries by region", or any metric "by region", use the depot\'s region (join delivery_runs → depots → regions). Do not use customer region; region means the operating region of the depot that fulfilled the delivery.\n', '\n', '- For "last month" use: scheduled_at >= add_months(DATE_TRUNC(\'month\', CURRENT_DATE),
                    -1) AND scheduled_at < DATE_TRUNC(\'month\', CURRENT_DATE). For "last quarter" use: scheduled_at >= add_months(DATE_TRUNC(\'quarter\', CURRENT_DATE),
                    -3) AND scheduled_at < DATE_TRUNC(\'quarter\', CURRENT_DATE). For "this year" use scheduled_at >= DATE_TRUNC(\'year\', CURRENT_DATE).\n', '\n', '- Prefer listing depot names and driver names (from depots.depot_name, drivers.driver_name) rather than IDs in results when the question asks "which depot" or "who".\n', '\n', '- Our regions are only North, South, East, and West. If the user asks about a different region (e.g. "Central",
                    "Midwest"), respond that we do not have that region and list the available regions: North, South, East, West.'
                ]
            }
        ], 'example_question_sqls': [
            {'id': '01f106b2d2fb1ccd88a13be4147e17d0', 'question': ['Who are the top 5 drivers by delivery count in the North region?'
                ], 'sql': ['SELECT d.driver_name, COUNT(*) AS delivery_count\n', 'FROM zg.genie_demo.delivery_runs r\n', 'JOIN zg.genie_demo.drivers d ON r.driver_id = d.driver_id\n', 'JOIN zg.genie_demo.depots dep ON d.depot_id = dep.depot_id\n', 'JOIN zg.genie_demo.regions reg ON dep.region_id = reg.region_id\n',
                    "WHERE r.status = 'delivered'\n", '  AND reg.region_name = :region_name\n', 'GROUP BY d.driver_id, d.driver_name\n', 'ORDER BY delivery_count DESC\n', 'LIMIT 5;'
                ], 'parameters': [
                    {'name': 'region_name', 'type_hint': 'STRING'
                    }
                ], 'usage_guidance': ['Use when the user asks for top drivers by delivery count in a specific region (e.g. North, South, East, West). Only count delivered runs. Fill :region_name with the region name from the question; it must match a value in regions.region_name.'
                ]
            },
            {'id': '01f10c3275331fad8583561cb4d7507a', 'question': ['How many on time deliveries did we complete last week?'
                ], 'sql': ['SELECT COUNT(*) AS on_time_delivery_count\n', 'FROM zg.genie_demo.delivery_runs\n',
